# Builds the documentation site (wiki/ -> GitHub Pages) and the in-panel Manual.
# MkDocs 2.0 drops the plugin and theme system Material depends on, so stay on 1.x.
#
# This is the INPUT. CI installs from requirements-docs.txt, the pip-compile
# output (exact versions + hashes, so a release job runs only the packages that
# were reviewed). Dependabot's pip updater recognises that pairing and
# regenerates the .txt with fresh hashes in its own PRs. After changing THIS
# file, regenerate and commit both:
#
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras --no-emit-index-url \
#     -o requirements-docs.txt requirements-docs.in
mkdocs>=1.6,<2
mkdocs-material>=9.6,<10
